<title>UK: Russian SBS-Agro to launch $150 mln three-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Russian SBS-Agro to launch $150 mln three-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian bank SBS-Agro (Stolichny Bank Sberegeny) will launch a three-year deal worth around $150 million next week, J.P. Morgan Securities said on Wednesday as lead manager.  </p>
<p>SBS-Agro, rated B1 by Moody's, B+ by S&amp;P and BB by IBCA, has been holding roadshows for the deal since June 24. The roadshows end today.</p>
<p>Price talk away from the lead manager covered a broad 350-450 basis points range.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
